diagnosis_text:
A full diagnostic sweep of the Kath2 topology found no fault, past or present, that matches the Office department's reported outage. Phase A triage (infra_sweep + l2_snapshot) confirmed zero ACL/firewall drop rules, zero duplicate MAC addresses, no IP/gateway/resolver misconfigurations, and no link anomalies across all 30 devices. Phase B confirmed the topology runs RIP (not OSPF); the ripd daemon is live on all three routers (PIDs confirmed), and every subnet — including 1.0.0.0/8 (Server Room) and 128.168.0.0/16 (Internet Lab) — has fresh, bidirectionally-learned RIP routes on router1 (the Office's gateway) and router2 (the Server Room/Internet gateway). Phase D (pressure_sweep) found no stress tools, CPU spikes, or socket storms on any device. Direct ICMP probes from office_pc and enquiry to pc1 (1.0.0.5, Server Room) and pc2 (128.168.0.2, Internet Lab) both returned 0% loss. Carrier-change counters on all router interfaces sit at 2 — the expected startup-only value in Kathara, with no evidence of subsequent link flaps. journalctl produced no entries, and dhcp_link_history surfaced no suspicious history. The user's report is unconfirmed: no mechanism or historical trace of the described isolation was found in the live lab, and the current state is fully healthy in every measured dimension.
=== END ===